# Commit Conventions

All commit messages must be written in **English** (see Language Policy).

## Format

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

### Type (required)

| Type       | When to use |
|------------|-------------|
| `feat`     | New feature or user-visible capability |
| `fix`      | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature |
| `test`     | Adding or updating tests only |
| `docs`     | Documentation only |
| `chore`    | Tooling, deps, CI — no production code behavior change |
| `perf`     | Performance improvement |
| `build`    | Build system or external dependency changes |
| `ci`       | CI/CD pipeline changes |
| `revert`   | Reverts a previous commit |

### Scope (recommended)

Short, lowercase layer or module name aligned with architecture:

`domain`, `application`, `infrastructure`, `api`, `ui`, `auth`, `db`, `deps`, `ci`

Omit scope only when the change is truly cross-cutting.

### Subject (required)

- Imperative mood: "add handler" not "added handler"
- Lowercase, no trailing period
- Max 72 characters
- Describe **why** or **what** at a glance — not implementation details

```
feat(domain): enforce unique chip invariant on registration
fix(api): return structured error for invalid state transition
test(domain): cover OwnershipTransferred event emission
```

## Body (when needed)

Use the body for:

- Business rule or use case reference (e.g., `BR-001`, `UC-RegisterAnimal`)
- Breaking changes
- Non-obvious rationale

Wrap at 72 characters. Separate subject from body with a blank line.

## Footer

- `BREAKING CHANGE: <description>` for breaking API or contract changes
- `Refs: #<issue>` when linked to a tracker issue

## Agent Commit Workflow

- **Only commit when the user explicitly asks** — never commit proactively
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys, tokens)
- Never skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless the user explicitly requests it
- Never force-push to `main`/`master`
- Prefer focused commits: one logical change per commit
- Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` before committing to match project style
- If a pre-commit hook fails, fix the issue and create a **new** commit — do not amend a failed commit

## Anti-Patterns

```
❌ fixed stuff
❌ WIP
❌ feat: mudanças no domínio
❌ update files
❌ feat(domain): refactored the entire codebase and also fixed unrelated bug
```
